B.O1=s(["An armed aircraft is never authorized by civil drone rules or by LAANC. Live-munitions employment runs entirely through the military chain: service and DoW authorizations, weapons safety and range control, and designated restricted/range airspace (or a specific FAA authorization for the operation).","One-way attack / loitering munitions are employed AS munitions under the same principle, whatever their weight class.","Governing publications and approval authorities (from the public DoW source map): military UAS fly as public aircraft under FAA Certificates of Authorization, not Part 107 (DoD OGC determination, 16 May 2019, cited in DAFMAN 11-501 \xb61.1). Air Force: AFPD 11-5 \u2192 DAFMAN 11-501 (approval chain AF/A3S \u2192 MAJCOM \u2192 installation \u2192 squadron \u2192 unit sUAS program manager). Army: AR 95-1. Navy/USMC: OPNAVINST 3710.7 + NAVAIRINST 13034.1 flight clearances; USMC NAVMC 3500.107. Space Force flies under the Air Force stack \u2014 it has no standalone UAS publications.","Shepherd names the governing framework and authorities only \u2014 it gives no employment guidance and clears nothing."],t.s)
